# ZFS Naming Rules

Use `docs/naming-conventions.md` as the project authority for every new or changed SAP artifact name.

- All custom objects begin with `ZFS` unless the naming document lists a human-approved exception.
- Validate DDIC, CDS/RAP, ABAP OO, package, service, binding, local class, message, and in-code names against the naming document before proposing or creating them.
- Before creating any SAP object, record `NAMING: <name> -> matches <pattern row | exception row>`.
- If the name does not match the pattern table or exception list, stop before creation and ask for a corrected or explicitly approved name.
- A copied, derived, successor, or variant object must conform independently. Never inherit a non-conforming source name.
- The project-wide message class is `ZFS_TEST_VS`; do not create or extend per-area message classes.
- For RAP business objects, use the VDM layering patterns in the naming document. The BO root view is `ZFS_R_<Entity>`, not `ZFS_I_<Entity>` or generic `ZI_`/`ZC_` prefixes.
